      },
      "worked": "The particles meet when their displacements are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}t^2+6&=\\frac{12t-t^2}{2}\\\\2t^2+12&=12t-t^2\\\\3t^2-12t+12&=0\\\\3(t-2)^2&=0\\\\t&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe repeated root gives exactly one meeting time. At that instant,\n$$\\begin{align*}v_A(t)&=\\frac{dx_A}{dt}=2t\\\\v_B(t)&=\\frac{dx_B}{dt}=6-t\\\\v_A(2)&=4\\text{ m s}^{-1}\\\\v_B(2)&=4\\text{ m s}^{-1}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth velocities are positive and equal, so the particles travel at the same speed, to the right.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
